**/profiling

# Development-only repository assets not used by this benchmark image
multi-robot-runtime-verification
robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/.devcontainer
robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/.github
robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/.githooks
robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/.vscode
robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/.zed
robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/.vimspector.json
robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/docs
robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/examples
robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/fixtures

robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/tests
robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/proptest-regressions
robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/docker
robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/scripts
robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/integrations/fmu

# The checker crate embeds these SVGs in Rust documentation at compile time.
!robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/docs/
!robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/docs/src/
!robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/docs/src/assets/
!robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/docs/src/assets/dataflow/
!robosapiens-trustworthiness-checker/docs/src/assets/dataflow/*.svg

# Top-level documentation is not needed at runtime; it remains in the source tree.
README.md
LICENSE.md
ICA-USAGE-MODE.txt

# The mstlo subtree feeds docker/Dockerfile.mstlo, so most of it has to stay in
# the context.  Two things do not:
#
#   paper_results/ is ~36 MB of figures and CSVs published with the RV26 paper.
#   Nothing in this image reads it, and the numbers it contains were measured
#   natively on macOS -- they are not what this image reproduces.
mstlo/benchmarks/synthetic_signal/paper_results
mstlo/_site
mstlo/cobertura.xml

# But the incubator's committed recording MUST stay: it is the signal that
# `run incubator` replays when no fresh gather has happened, which is what makes
# that benchmark work out of the box.  Spelled out because the broad **/results
# and **/report rules above are easy to extend into it by accident.
!mstlo/benchmarks/incubator/data
!mstlo/benchmarks/incubator/data/**

# The incubator course and the digital twin it vendors are ~180 MB, almost all
# of it recorded experiment data and documentation that the gather stage never
# touches.  It needs the `incubator` Python package, startup.conf, and the two
# requirements files; nothing here is imported outside the upstream test suite.
example-digital-twin-incubator/notes
example-digital-twin-incubator/figures
example-digital-twin-incubator/software/docs
example-digital-twin-incubator/software/incubator/datasets
example-digital-twin-incubator/software/incubator/tests
example-digital-twin-incubator/software/integration_tests

# The course keeps its submodule pointer at this path; the real content is
# vendored as example-digital-twin-incubator and copied in by the Dockerfile.
incubator-dt-course/incubator_dt
